{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-106-1","title":"Psalms 106:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The psalmist exhorts to praise God. 4 He prays for pardon of sin, as God pardoned the fathers. 7 The story of the people's rebellion, and God's mercy. 47 He concludes with prayer and praise.</p>\n<p>(Title.)As part of the preceding Psalm is found in 1 Ch ch. 16, so the first and two last verses of this are found in the same place; and it is highly probable this was composed upon the same occasion as the former, to which it seems to be a continuation; for as that celebrates the mercies of God to Israel, so this confesses and deplores the rebellions of Israel against Jehovah.</p>\n<p>Praise ye the Lord. Heb. Hallelujah. 105:45 O give. 100:4,5; 107:1; 118:1; 136:1; 1Ch 16:34; Ezr 3:11; Jer 33:11 1Th 5:18 for he. 103:17; 119:68; Mt 19:17; Ro 5:20,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-2","title":"Psalms 106:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>utter. 40:5; 139:17,18; 145:3-12; Job 5:9; 26:14; Ro 11:33; Eph 1:19; 3:18 all his praise. Ne 9:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-3","title":"Psalms 106:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Blessed. 1:1-3; 84:11,12; 119:1-3; Mr 3:35; Lu 6:47-49; 11:28; Joh 13:17 Joh 15:14; Jas 1:25; Re 7:15; 22:14 keep. 119:106; Isa 56:1,2; Jer 22:15,16; Lu 11:42; Joh 14:21-23 doeth. 15:2; 119:44; Isa 64:5; Eze 18:21,22; Lu 1:74,75; Ac 24:16; Ro 2:7 Ga 6:9; Re 22:14 at all times. 119:20,112; De 5:19; 11:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-4","title":"Psalms 106:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Remember. 25:7; 119:132; Ne 5:19; 13:14,22,31; Lu 23:42 visit. Lu 1:68,69; Ac 15:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-5","title":"Psalms 106:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>may see. 105:6,43; De 7:6; Joh 15:16; Ac 9:15; Eph 1:4; 2Th 2:13; Jas 2:5 1Pe 2:9; Re 17:14 rejoice. 14:7; 48:11; Isa 12:6; 35:10; 66:10; Joe 2:23; Zep 3:14; Zec 9:9 Joh 16:22; Php 3:3 glory. Isa 45:25; Eph 1:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-6","title":"Psalms 106:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>78:8; Le 26:40; Nu 32:14; 1Ki 8:47; Ezr 9:6,7; Ne 9:16,32-34 Da 9:5-8; Mt 23:32; Ac 7:51,52</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-7","title":"Psalms 106:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Our. De 29:4; 32:28,29; Pr 1:22; Isa 44:18; Mr 4:12; 8:17-21 2Th 2:10-12 they. 78:42; 105:5; De 15:15; Eph 2:11 multitude. 45; 5:7; 51:1; Isa 63:7; La 3:32 but. Ex 14:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-8","title":"Psalms 106:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>he saved. 143:11; Nu 14:13-16; De 32:26,27; Jos 7:9; Jer 14:7,21 Eze 20:9,14,22,44; Da 9:17-19 that he. 111:6; Ex 9:16; 15:6; Ro 9:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-9","title":"Psalms 106:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>He rebuked.In the descriptions of the Psalmist, everything has life. The sea is an animated being, behaves itself proudly, is rebuked, and retires in confusion.</p>\n<p>18:15; 66:6; 78:13,52,53; 114:3-7; 136:13-16; Ex 14:21,22,27-29 Ne 9:11; Isa 11:14-16; Na 1:4; Mt 8:26 so he. 77:19,20; Isa 63:11-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-10","title":"Psalms 106:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>And he. Ex 14:30; 15:9,10; De 11:4; Ne 9:11 redeemed. 107:2; 136:24; Ex 15:13; Job 6:22,23; Mic 6:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-11","title":"Psalms 106:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>78:53; Ex 14:13,27,28; 15:5,10,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-12","title":"Psalms 106:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Ex 14:31; 15:1-21; Lu 8:13; Joh 8:30,31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-13","title":"Psalms 106:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>They soon forgat. Heb. They made haste, they forgat.Three days afterwards, at the waters of Marah.</p>\n<p>78:11; Ex 15:17,24; 16:2; 17:7 waited. Pr 1:25,30; Isa 48:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-14","title":"Psalms 106:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>But. 78:18,30; Nu 11:4,33,34; De 9:22; 1Co 10:6 lusted exceedingly. Heb. lusted a lust. tempted. 78:18-20,40,41; 95:8,9; Ex 17:2; Nu 14:22; 1Co 10:9; Heb 3:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-15","title":"Psalms 106:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>he gave. 78:29-31; Nu 11:31-34; Isa 10:16; 24:16 but sent.They despised the manna, calling it light or innutritive food. God gave them flesh as they desired, but no blessing accompanied it; and, in consequence, they did not fatten, but grew lean upon it; and many, surfeited by excess, died of disease. Instead of {razon,} \"leanness,\" however, Bp. Lowth supposes we should read {zera�n,} \"nausea or loathing,\" which appears to be supported by several ancient versions, and by Nu 11:20, where this portion of the history of the Israelites is recorded, and where the word {zara} is used, and rendered, \"it be loathsome.\"</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-16","title":"Psalms 106:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>envied. Nu 16:1,3-50 the saint. Ex 28:36; Le 21:6-8,10-12; Nu 16:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-17","title":"Psalms 106:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Nu 16:29-33; 26:10; De 11:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-18","title":"Psalms 106:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Nu 16:35-40,46; Heb 12:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-19","title":"Psalms 106:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Ex 32:4-8,35; De 9:12-16,21; Ne 9:18; 1Co 10:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-20","title":"Psalms 106:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Thus. 89:17; Jer 2:11; Ro 1:22,23 their glory.That is, their God, who ought to have been the peculiar object of their glory.</p>\n<p>into. Ex 20:4,5; Isa 40:18-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-21","title":"Psalms 106:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>forgat. 13; 78:11,12,42-51; De 32:17,18; Jer 2:32 God. Isa 12:2; 45:21; 63:8; Ho 1:7; Lu 1:47; Tit 1:3; 2:10; 3:4-6 which. 74:13,14; 135:9; De 4:34; 6:22; 7:18,19; Ne 9:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-22","title":"Psalms 106:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Wondrous.The plagues he inflicted on the Egyptians. Egypt is called the land of Ham, or rather, Cham, because it was peopled by Mizraim the son of Ham, and grandson of Noah. Plutarch informs us, that the Egyptians called their country [Chemia,] Chemia; and the Copts give it the name of Chemi, [Chemi,] to the present day.</p>\n<p>78:51; 105:23,27-36 terrible. Ex 14:25-28; 15:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-23","title":"Psalms 106:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>he said. Ex 32:10,11,32; De 9:13,14,19,25; 10:10; Eze 20:13,14 his chosen. 105:6,26; Nu 16:5; Mt 12:18; Joh 15:16,19 stood. Ex 32:14; Jer 5:1; Eze 13:5; 22:30; Jas 5:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-24","title":"Psalms 106:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>they despised. Ge 25:34; Nu 13:32; 14:31; Mt 22:5; Heb 12:16 the pleasant land. Heb. a land of desire. De 8:7-9; 11:11,12; Jer 3:19; Eze 20:6 they believed. Nu 14:11; De 1:32; Heb 3:12,18,19; 4:2,6,14; Jude 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-25","title":"Psalms 106:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>murmured. Nu 14:1-4,27-29; De 1:26,27 hearkened. 95:7-9; Nu 14:22; Heb 3:7,8,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-26","title":"Psalms 106:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>Therefore. 95:11; Nu 14:28-35; De 1:34,35; Heb 3:11,18 lifted. Ge 14:22,23; Ex 6:8; De 32:40-42; Eze 20:15; Re 10:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-27","title":"Psalms 106:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>overthrow. Heb. make them fall. to scatter. 44:11; Le 26:33; De 4:26,27; 28:37,64,65; 32:26,27; Eze 20:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-28","title":"Psalms 106:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>joined. Nu 25:1-3,5; 31:16; De 4:3; 32:17; Jos 22:17; Ho 9:10; Re 2:14 of the dead.The word {maithim} signifies dead men; for the idols of the heathen were generally men,--warriors, kings, or lawgivers,-- who had been deified after their death; though many of them had been execrated during their life.</p>\n<p>115:4-8; Jer 10:8-10; 1Co 10:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-29","title":"Psalms 106:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>with their. 39; 99:8; De 32:16-21; Ec 7:29; Ro 1:21-24 the plague. Nu 25:9; 1Co 10:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-30","title":"Psalms 106:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Nu 25:6-8,14,15; De 13:9-11,15-17; Jos 7:12; 1Ki 18:40,41 Jon 1:12-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-31","title":"Psalms 106:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>Nu 25:11-13; De 24:13; Mr 14:3-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-32","title":"Psalms 106:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>angered. 78:40; 81:7; Nu 20:2,6,13 so that. Nu 20:12,23,24; 27:13,14; De 1:37; 3:26; 4:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-33","title":"Psalms 106:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>Because. Nu 20:10,11 he spake. 39:1; 141:3; Ge 30:1; 35:16-18; Job 2:10; 38:2; 40:4,5; 42:7,8 Jas 3:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-34","title":"Psalms 106:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>did not. Jos 15:63; 16:10; 17:12-16; 23:12,13; Jud 1:19,21,27-35 Mt 17:19-21 concerning. Nu 33:52,55,56; De 7:2,16,23,24; 20:16,17; 1Sa 15:3,22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-35","title":"Psalms 106:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>But. Jos 15:63; Jud 1:27-36; 2:2,3 learned. Isa 2:6; 1Co 5:6; 15:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-36","title":"Psalms 106:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>And. 78:58; Ex 34:15,16; Jud 2:12,13,17,19; 3:5-7; 10:6 2Ki 17:8-11,16,17; 2Ch 33:2-9; Eze 16:15-63; 20:28-32 which. Ex 23:33; De 7:16; Jos 23:13; Jud 2:3,14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-37","title":"Psalms 106:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>they sacrificed.However unnatural and horrid human sacrifices may appear, it is certain, that they did not only exist, but almost universally prevailed in the heathen world, especially among the Canaanites and Phoenicians.</p>\n<p>De 12:30,31; 18:10; 2Ki 16:3; 17:17; 21:6; Isa 57:5; Jer 7:31; 32:35 Eze 16:20,21; 20:26; 23:37,47 devils. Le 17:7; De 32:17; 2Ch 11:15; 1Co 10:20; Ro 9:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-38","title":"Psalms 106:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>shed. De 21:9; 2Ki 21:16; 24:4; Jer 2:34 the land. Nu 35:33; Isa 1:15; 26:21; Eze 7:23; 22:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-39","title":"Psalms 106:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>defiled. Isa 24:5,6; 59:3; Eze 20:18,30,31,43 went. Ex 34:16; Le 17:7; 20:5,6; Nu 15:39; Jer 3:1,2,6-9; Eze 16:15-63 Eze 23:3-49; Ho 9:1; Re 17:1-6 their own. 29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-40","title":"Psalms 106:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>the wrath. 78:59-62; Jud 2:14,20; 3:8; Ne 9:27-38 insomuch. Le 20:23; De 32:19; Zec 11:8 his own. 74:1; De 9:29; La 2:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-41","title":"Psalms 106:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>he gave. De 32:30; Jud 2:14; 3:8,12; 4:1,2; 6:1-6; 10:7-18; Ne 9:27-38 and they. De 28:25,29,33,48</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-43","title":"Psalms 106:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>Many. Jud 2:16-18; 1Sa 12:9-11 with their. 29; 1:1; 81:12 brought low. or, impoverished, or weakened. Jud 5:8; 6:5; 1Sa 13:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-44","title":"Psalms 106:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>Jud 2:18; 3:9; 4:3; 6:6-10; 10:10-16; 1Sa 7:8-12; 2Ki 14:26,27 Ne 9:27-38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-45","title":"Psalms 106:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>And he. 105:8; Le 26:40-42; 2Ki 13:23; Lu 1:71,72 repented. 90:13; 135:14; Ex 32:14; De 32:36; Jud 2:18; 2Sa 24:16; Ho 11:8 Am 7:3,6 to the. 51:1; 69:16; Isa 63:7; La 3:32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-46","title":"Psalms 106:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>1Ki 8:50; Ezr 9:9; Jer 15:11; 42:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-47","title":"Psalms 106:47","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":47,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":47},"content":"<p>Save us. 14:7; 126:1; 1Ch 16:35 gather. Jer 32:37-41; Eze 36:24-28; 37:21-28; 39:25-29 to give. 107:1-3; 2Co 2:14; Re 7:10-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-106-48","title":"Psalms 106:48","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":106,"verseStart":48,"chapterEnd":106,"verseEnd":48},"content":"<p>Blessed. 41:13; 72:18,19; 89:52; 1Ch 29:10; 1Co 14:16 Praise ye the Lord. Heb. Hallelujah. 1; 105:45; *marg:</p>"}]}